# Exercises the Support Assistant against the compose stack (`make up`), as the demo Customer,
# directly and through the gateway. Run the token request first; it stores the token for the ones
# after it. With the anthropic-api-key secret empty, as `make secrets` (which `make up` runs) writes it, the mock provider
# answers. Asked where their Order is, it names the demo Customer's latest Order, or says they have
# none: check one out in the Storefront first to see it. 12 of its messages count against the demo
# Customer's 20 an hour, so a second run within the hour ends in 429 assistantRateLimited.

@assistant = http://localhost:8102
@gateway = http://localhost:8000
@keycloak = http://localhost:8180/realms/ecomm/protocol/openid-connect/token

### The demo Customer's token
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=dev-cli&username=demo@ecomm.local&password=demo

> {% client.global.set("customerToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### Start a Conversation: 201, empty
POST {{assistant}}/conversations
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

> {% client.global.set("conversationId", response.body.id); %}

### Ask where their Order is: the reply names the latest Order and its Shipment, and references it
POST {{assistant}}/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"text": "Where is my order?"}

> {% client.global.set("orderReference", response.body.references.length ? response.body.references[0].reference : "#00000000"); %}

### Ask about it by its Order reference: found among the Customer's Orders, or not found among them
POST {{assistant}}/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"text": "Where is my order {{orderReference}}?"}

### Ask about a charge: the Payment transaction history, an Authorization explained as a hold
POST {{assistant}}/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"text": "Why was I charged twice?"}

### Ask about a Refund: its amount and what it was for, or that there is none
POST {{assistant}}/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"text": "Has my refund gone through?"}

### Ask about an RMA by its RMA reference: its status and next step, or not found among theirs
POST {{assistant}}/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"text": "What's happening with RMA-3F2A9C1B?"}

### Ask whether the latest Order can still be returned: until when, and its page to request one
POST {{assistant}}/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"text": "Can I still return my order?"}

### Ask where their returns are: the one explained, several listed, or none
POST {{assistant}}/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"text": "Where is my return?"}

### Ask whether a Product is in Stock in a Variant: its Stock and Price, linked to its page
POST {{assistant}}/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"text": "Is the Pixel 9 in 256 GB in stock?"}

### Ask about a Product's Warranty terms
POST {{assistant}}/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"text": "Does the Pixel 9 come with a warranty?"}

### Ask for Products that fit a need: a few, each with its Price
POST {{assistant}}/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"text": "I'm looking for noise cancelling headphones"}

### Ask something else: answered without a lookup
POST {{assistant}}/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"text": "Hello!"}

### An empty message: 400 invalidMessage
POST {{assistant}}/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"text": ""}

### Ask with an Idempotency-Key, unique to this Conversation: the reply, as for any message
POST {{assistant}}/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: http-file-{{conversationId}}

{"text": "Where is my order?"}

### The same again: the same reply, with no turn run and nothing added to the transcript
POST {{assistant}}/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: http-file-{{conversationId}}

{"text": "Where is my order?"}

### The transcript, through the gateway
GET {{gateway}}/api/support-assistant/conversations/{{conversationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### End it: 204
DELETE {{assistant}}/conversations/{{conversationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Ended, it is gone: 404
GET {{assistant}}/conversations/{{conversationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
